        "results": {
          "reviewResult": "{\"summary\":\"Phase 1: analyzing 1 input group(s) with failures (cap 1 failed input(s) by settings; 2 unmatched comparison row(s) in scope); each prompt includes every comparison row for that input (matched + unmatched). Phase 1.5: if more than 5 Phase-1 issues, cluster related issues (one LLM call; fallback: group by category hint); if ≤5 issues, one cluster per issue (no clustering LLM). Phase 2: one prompt-edit per cluster (sequential; one merged edit fixes all cases in the cluster); duplicate spans across clusters are deduped once.\",\"suggestions\":[{\"name\":\"Prompt edit\",\"phase1_addresses\":[\"No output was generated\",\"The model did not produce any output for the given input.\"],\"old_sentence\":\"Return exactly one label: positive, negative, or neutral. Do not include an explanation.\",\"new_sentence\":\"Return exactly one label: positive, negative, or neutral. If no sentiment is clearly discernible, return neutral. Do not include an explanation.\",\"reason\":\"The model is not returning any output. To ensure a label is always generated, explicitly instruct the model to return 'neutral' if the sentiment is not clearly discernible.\",\"target_score_row_indices\":[0,2],\"row_indices\":[0,2],\"issue_cluster_index\":0,\"issue_cluster_label\":\"no-output\",\"source\":\"pipeline\",\"suggestion_id\":1,\"applied\":true}],\"data_refinement\":[],\"row_diagnostics\":[{\"input_index\":1,\"row_indices\":[0,2],\"card_title\":\"No output was generated\",\"issue_summary\":\"The model did not produce any output for the given input. The expected output was a single label 'positive'.\",\"rough_modification_opinion\":\"The prompt should be more explicit about the requirement to always return a label, even if it's 'neutral' when unsure. Adding a rule like 'If no sentiment is clearly discernible, return neutral.' might help.\",\"problem_category_hint\":\"no-output\",\"gt_suspect_note\":\"\"}],\"promptSections\":[{\"name\":\"Task\",\"content\":\"Cl